Z||000015||Cliff Pennock||08-20-2001||08:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85ZainoGT:<BR><B>Who thinks this is a slow forum?  example, I can get on here and look @ tech, general, and the mall, and come back in anywhere from 3-8 hours, with the SAME stuff still there pretty much, maybe 2 or 3 new things...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Me thinks you have a problem with AOL's caching. On the average, there are anywhere between 500-2000 new messages every day. Problem with AOL is, that it retrieves most of it out of its own cache (proxy). And unfortunately it can take anywhere between 5 minutes and half a day before AOL updates its proxy.<P>I just noticed that problem when I was in the States. My sister has an AOL account next to her normal internet account and when I browsed the forum using AOL, it was typically a few hours behind.<P>People here are fast to reply. Just check the time you posted this message and then the times people posted their response! Slow you say?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||stimpy||08-20-2001||08:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85ZainoGT:<BR><B>we need more participation in the forum... that means we need to go out and find the fiero guys that dont know about the forum   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> |</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think more important is to find people who have something to say. I used to spend a lot of time here, making plenty of posts.  It's gottento be that with my lame-ass WebTV, it's just not worth it to wade through image-laden threads and topics that were boring he first 20 times they were posted (Yes, we all know Fieros were in the Star Trek movie. Yawn) And I think there are probably others that feel the same. (GTbastard and Black88GT, can I get a witness?)<P>Not this isn't meant to be a rant against the forum, but the newness of the toy has worn off for a lot of us veteranos.  It's up to the new blood to make it or break it for yourselves.  I know that my tech questions get an answer usually in half hour, not just because people know me, but I make the titles of my topics descriptive and give plenty of info. Topics called "Help" are gonna get a pass every time.<BR>||209.240.220.149||reg||1
Z||000017||ChadMan||08-20-2001||09:48 AM||||If you want a fast response, just post something about FieroLisa, religion, or politics.||||reg||12
Z||000018||DXR_DAD||08-20-2001||11:07 AM||||stimpy & Al, you both have good points!!!<BR>I've been here from the start of PFF and at the start it was the place to be, still is!!! but there are so many question that are asked over and over again, I don't ask a lot of question most ot the time I use the SEARCH,<BR>Ogre's Cave and the ARCHIVES. Yes I think Stimpy is right about the new members taking up the slack  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>With so many projects going on at the same time now it's hard to just stay here and chat. But the O/T section is booming!!! I think there are some that live there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It's still the best place for Fiero info!!!<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||4
